+- Candidates may change only auto- or text-tier options, within allowed values and respecting requires. Never touch frozen options. Each candidate is one configuration relative to the current version, even if it changes several options. Follow the enforced output format and candidate-count limit.
+- For custom_notes, choose an available trigger and write one short sentence appended when it fires. Skills are short, optional how-to documents containing only general terminal-working advice. Do not include task-specific content, expected output formats, tests, grading, or answers. Text is screened and human-approved.
+- Prefer mechanisms that do not consume model turns under a hard time limit. Do not assume that extra verification pays for itself.
+- Before proposing an efficiency change, check how often its target behavior occurs and how much total cost it can possibly remove. Compare that upper bound with the relevant statistical-gate threshold. Withdraw ideas with insufficient headroom rather than predicting gains from a large change to a rare behavior. [v0+c01, v0+c02]
+- For combinations, estimate total headroom from the component behaviors without double-counting. Do not use a combination to rescue components whose combined upper bound is still too small; say what distinct interaction would make it different if proposing one. [v0+c01, v0+c02, v0+c03]
+- Separate the direct mechanism, overall turns and tokens, wall-clock time, and passes in predictions. A large reduction in a targeted behavior does not establish a time or pass improvement. Predict each outcome conservatively and allow zero pass change when appropriate. [v0+c04]
